    "analysis": "The Brazil government bond market offers attractive yields compared to global standards, but with higher credit risk. To maintain our fixed income portfolio's current average duration of 8.2 years and within the max_duration_years constraint of 10, I propose reducing the allocation to Brazil bonds. Additionally, due to their higher credit risk, we should prioritize bonds with good credit ratings. A laddered maturity structure should be maintained for added stability; specifically, for a 10-year portfolio with the constraint of not more than 30% maturing in any single year, I suggest allocating 25% to 2-year bonds, 20% to 5-year bonds, and 30% to 7-year bonds, with the remaining 25% in the next bucket, i.e., 10-year bonds. This allocation will require a reweighting of the current portfolio.",
